msgid "**Audit ingest:** A throwaway instance spools audit entries locally and sends them with its own sequence numbers; the live provisioner assigns time, sequence and a hash-chained link (``utils.orchestrator.audit``), reports gaps in the spooled sequence, and keeps the chain insert-only so a later edit or deletion is detectable."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Audit ingest:** A throwaway instance spools audit entries locally and sends them with its own sequence numbers; the live provisioner assigns time, sequence and a hash-chained link (`utils.orchestrator.audit`), reports gaps in the spooled sequence, and keeps the chain insert-only so a later edit or deletion is detectable."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Audit trail:** A ``file`` audit device at ``stdout/``, declared in the server config, writes every request, with the accessing identity and a timestamp, to the server’s stdout and so to the container log. Secret values appear only as salted HMACs. Every deploy reads a probe secret and fails unless the log shows that read with its identity and time."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Audit trail:** A `file` audit device at `stdout/`, declared in the server config, writes every request, with the accessing identity and a timestamp, to the server's stdout and so to the container log. Secret values appear only as salted HMACs. Every deploy reads a probe secret and fails unless the log shows that read with its identity and time."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Audit:** the realm records admin events, so every membership the service grants appears under the approver who confirmed it, for as many days as ``services.keycloak.events.admin.expiration_days`` of `web-app-keycloak <../web-app-keycloak/README.md>`__ sets."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Audit:** the realm records admin events, so every membership the service grants appears under the approver who confirmed it, for as many days as `services.keycloak.events.admin.expiration_days` of [web-app-keycloak](../web-app-keycloak/README.md) sets."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Auth caveat is documented.** Home Assistant uses its own auth (users + long-lived tokens + `trusted_proxies`), not full OIDC. The MCP endpoint is authenticated with a Home Assistant credential stored in `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:`; if platform SSO in front of the HA UI is wanted, the trusted-proxy header approach and its limits MUST be documented in the role README."
msgstr "**Auth の洞窟は文書化されます。** ホームアシスタントは、独自のauthを使用しています (ユーザー+長期トークン+ `trusted_proxies`), OIDC を満たさない MCP エンドポイントは、MCP エンドポイントが認証されます。 Home Assistant 保存された認証 `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:`; HA UIの前でプラットフォームSSOが必要な場合は、信頼できるプロキシヘッダーのアプローチと、その制限は、READMEの役割で文書化される必要があります。."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Auth:** \"Sign in with Bluesky\" — AT Protocol OAuth against the user's PDS / identity. No local password store."
msgstr "**認証:** \"サインイン Bluesky\" — ユーザのPDS / IDに対するプロトコルOAuth。 ローカルパスワードストアはありません。."

msgid "**Authenticated push:** ``loki.write`` sends to ``https://loki.<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>/loki/api/v1/push`` with the ``push_token`` of ``web-svc-loki`` as bearer token, read from the ``0600`` env file, and with the tenant header ``X-Scope-OrgID``. Pushes retry with backoff (``services.svc-log-collector.push``) while Loki is not reachable."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Authenticated push:** `loki.write` sends to `https://loki.<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>/loki/api/v1/push` with the `push_token` of `web-svc-loki` as bearer token, read from the `0600` env file, and with the tenant header `X-Scope-OrgID`. Pushes retry with backoff (`services.svc-log-collector.push`) while Loki is not reachable."
