msgid "The dashboard signs in through its own public Keycloak client (PKCE S256, no service account, declared under ``services.sso.oidc.clients`` of ``web-app-dashboard``). Only that client’s access tokens carry the ``allowed-origins`` claim, which the Account REST API needs to answer the dashboard’s cross-origin calls; the shared client and the realm’s ``web-origins`` scope keep the claim out of every other access token. When an Account REST call fails, times out or answers with a non-2xx status, the dashboard still runs “Log out on this device” and, after the redirect back, tells the user that other devices may still be signed in. Neither choice uses a Keycloak service account, a ``realm-management`` role, the Keycloak admin REST API, stored realm events or a Keycloak extension."
