msgid "With OIDC enabled, every Mailu service runs its Mailu-OIDC image except the webmail, which runs the upstream `ghcr.io/mailu/webmail` image."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SMTP (``lookup('email', 'web-app-keycloak').enabled``), the realm sets ``verifyEmail: true``, also on an existing realm at every deploy. A user whose address is not verified gets ``VERIFY_EMAIL`` at the next browser sign-in and receives a token only after following the link. A user without any address is not held. A password (direct) grant of such a user fails with ``Account is not fully set up`` until the address is verified; a client credentials grant of a service account evaluates no required action and is not affected."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SMTP (`lookup('email', 'web-app-keycloak').enabled`), the realm sets `verifyEmail: true`, also on an existing realm at every deploy. A user whose address is not verified gets `VERIFY_EMAIL` at the next browser sign-in and receives a token only after following the link. A user without any address is not held. A password (direct) grant of such a user fails with `Account is not fully set up` until the address is verified; a client credentials grant of a service account evaluates no required action and is not affected."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SMTP, a user changes the changeable address through `UPDATE_EMAIL` with forced verification: the new address takes effect after the user follows the link sent to it. Without SMTP only an administrator can change it."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SMTP, a user changes the changeable address through ``UPDATE_EMAIL`` with forced verification: the new address takes effect after the user follows the link sent to it. Without SMTP only an administrator can change it."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SSO disabled the role uses the Internal directory and the bot's derived account password."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SSO disabled the role uses the Internal directory and the bot’s derived account password."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SSO enabled the role creates every account without a password credential and sends no password update, so an account that already exists keeps the credentials it holds."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SSO on, the platform administrator is a GitLab-auth account and the password form is off. The local administrator keeps ``mmctl --local`` inside the ``mattermost`` container, which talks to the server over its local socket without signing in, for example ``mmctl --local user change-password`` or ``mmctl --local roles system-admin``. The environment overrides of ``templates/env.j2`` lock the sign-in settings, so bringing the form back takes ``services.mattermost.login.method.native.enabled: true`` in the inventory and a redeploy."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SSO on, the platform administrator is a GitLab-auth account and the password form is off. The local administrator keeps `mmctl --local` inside the `mattermost` container, which talks to the server over its local socket without signing in, for example `mmctl --local user change-password` or `mmctl --local roles system-admin`. The environment overrides of `templates/env.j2` lock the sign-in settings, so bringing the form back takes `services.mattermost.login.method.native.enabled: true` in the inventory and a redeploy."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SSO on, the second factor lives in Keycloak, so the application's own one is off. The realm sends every account without a second factor to TOTP enrollment through `services.keycloak.realm.totp_enforced` of `web-app-keycloak` (default `true`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SSO on, the shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys run: the OAuth source registers or auto-links their Gitea accounts at the first sign-in. Without SSO they are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``, because the shared native persona path probes ``/``, ``/login``, ``/admin`` and ``/accounts/login/`` for a password field while Gitea serves its form at ``/user/login`` only."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SSO on, the shared `biber` and `administrator` persona journeys run: the OAuth source registers or auto-links their Gitea accounts at the first sign-in. Without SSO they are opted out via `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` / `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2`, because the shared native persona path probes `/`, `/login`, `/admin` and `/accounts/login/` for a password field while Gitea serves its form at `/user/login` only."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SSO only ``sso``; without SSO but with LDAP ``ldap`` and ``2fa``; with neither ``native`` and ``2fa``. Every extra method is off."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SSO the administrator signs in through pgAdmin's own OAuth2 button, and [`files/playwright/test-rbac-roles.js`](./files/playwright/test-rbac-roles.js) drives that journey; without SSO pgAdmin's only login id is the internal e-mail `PGADMIN_DEFAULT_EMAIL` ([`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2), [`vars/main.yml`](./vars/main.yml)), not the Keycloak username. `OAUTH2_ADDITIONAL_CLAIMS` admits only the `administrator` and `user` RBAC groups, and `biber` carries an empty role list, so pgAdmin refuses it after the Keycloak login; the same spec asserts that refusal and the admission through the `user` group. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) therefore declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; the `guest` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr ""

msgid "With SSO the administrator signs in through pgAdmin’s own OAuth2 button, and ```files/playwright/test-rbac-roles.js`` <./files/playwright/test-rbac-roles.js>`__ drives that journey; without SSO pgAdmin’s only login id is the internal e-mail ``PGADMIN_DEFAULT_EMAIL`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__, ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__), not the Keycloak username. ``OAUTH2_ADDITIONAL_CLAIMS`` admits only the ``administrator`` and ``user`` RBAC groups, and ``biber`` carries an empty role list, so pgAdmin refuses it after the Keycloak login; the same spec asserts that refusal and the admission through the ``user`` group. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the ``guest`` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
